<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Venta Silurum</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Venta Silurum was the Roman town at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caerwent">Caerwent</a> in south-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>, capital of the civitas of the Silures after their conquest in the 70s CE. It had a forum, basilica, temples and baths, and later strong stone walls that still stand. An inscription found there records the council of the Silures governing the town. The name of Gwent, the post-Roman kingdom of the region, derives from Venta.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/venta-silurum.jpg" alt="Venta Silurum" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MortimerCat · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CaerwentWall.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
